select 'acids-bases', 'Henderson–Hasselbalch equation: Application to bases', 'is an association constant, Kb, which is simply related to the dissociation constant of the conjugate acid, BH+. is ca. 14 at 25 °C. This approximation can be used when the correct value is not known. Thus, the Henderson–Hasselbalch equation can be used, without modification, for bases.', 'Wikipedia: Henderson–Hasselbalch equation', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Henderson%E2%80%93Hasselbalch_equation&oldid=1381152166', 'CC BY-SA 4.0. Wikipedia contributors (see page history). Excerpted and split into passages.'
